  "description": "NIRJEH crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C52 H64 Er4 N4 O24,2(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er1A (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er2A (Er) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.542-3.731 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.96-104.46°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Er4(NO3)2(acac)4(L)2(CH3OH)2]·2CH3CN (C56H70Er4N6O24). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
